// `record` was the word until v0.0.148. It redirects rather than simply failing, because a
// rename a reader cannot see the reason for is a rename they will resent — and this one has a
// reason worth reading: a record held only fields, so everything you could DO with one lived
// somewhere else. Writing the same point-of-sale in Burxt, Python, PHP and Rust made the cost
// plain, and this was the largest readability gap of the four.
record Book { title: String }
